{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Problems and Solutions"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "An Advanced Copy: ARC"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le12ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Present Perfect Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense when you want to refer to the result of an action in the past that is important in the present. This is useful when you want to comment on the present results of something in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense, you think of the past and present together. There is some connection to what happened in the past and the situation in the present moment."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">have made</span> dinner. </span><br>You are referring to a past action (making dinner) that has a present result (dinner is ready to eat)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In a business context, you can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect Tense</span> to make observations about someone's performance or work."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">has adjusted</span> all of the visual stuff, like the illustration and caption issues that were pointed out last month. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take a look at some more examples from the dialogue:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I see you've received your advanced copy of the manuscript already."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Have you had a chance to look at it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have found that many of the suggested edits were ignored."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have been looking it over since this morning, and I am a little bit preoccupied with the results."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Report Verbs with Impersonal Passive Constructions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Some verbs you can use,  when you report what other people think or say, are <span class=\"italic\">claim, mention, request and point out</span>. These are especially useful in business contexts when presenting facts and opinions about work-related subjects. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you want to report a general comment or observation, you can use an impersonal passive construction. This means that you do not mention a person or group of people as the subject of the sentence, but rather use phrases like <span class=\"italic\">It was mentioned</span> or <span class=\"italic\">It is believed</span>. This style of speaking or writing is more academic sounding and used in workplace environments more than in everyday conversations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br><span class=\"italic\">Well, it <span class=\"strong\">was mentioned </span>that a few of the more complicated words should be removed, but not one of them was omitted. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "These errors were pointed out by our proofreaders ages ago."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was claimed that not enough feedback was received. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "These changes were requested on multiple occasions, and they were completely ignored."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "manuscript "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the original copy of a book, before it has been printed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I see you've received your advanced copy of the manuscript already."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when reviewing a document."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "advanced copy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a copy received before the official release date"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The advanced copy will arrive three weeks before the official release. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proofreader "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "somebody who checks a text for mistakes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These errors were pointed out by our proofreaders ages ago."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "at first glance\t"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " your first impression of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: At first glance it looked okay, but upon closer inspection, I have found that many of the suggested edits were ignored."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to omit "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to leave something out"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: it was mentioned that a few of the more complicated words should be removed, but not one of them was omitted."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le12ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to take out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to remove"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, 